# =============================================================================
# Auto-Company — runtime.env TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
# The live loop reads runtime overrides from  logs/runtime.env  (a persistent
# volume, NOT committed — logs/ is gitignored). This .example is the tracked
# reference so a fresh clone + deploy knows every knob and secret the loop uses.
#
# On a fresh deploy, provide these values one of two ways:
#   1) copy this file to  logs/runtime.env  and fill it in, OR
#   2) set them as Coolify container env vars (PID1 env; e.g. CONTEXT7_API_KEY
#      is provided this way today).
# Either layer feeds the loop's environment; runtime.env wins as an override.
#
# Format: literal  KEY=value  per line (docker-entrypoint.sh parses it directly,
# never `. source`s it — so values with shell-special chars like `|` are safe).
# NEVER commit real secret values. The cockpit "Settings — Runtime Config" panel
# only edits the NON-SECRET knobs below and preserves everything else.
# =============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# NON-SECRET operator knobs (editable in the cockpit Settings panel)
# Values below are the current tuned defaults — safe to ship as-is.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Opportunity Discovery — scan brand-new candidate axes: 1 = on, 0/blank = off.
# When off, auto-loop.sh's per-cycle prompt is instructed to focus on the
# tender track (see PROMPT.md -> TENDER TRACK) and improving 176-R instead of
# generating new candidates. Default when unset is OFF (operator decision,
# 2026-07-27) -- this differs from the other bool knobs below, which default
# to their prior standing behavior when blank.
DISCOVERY_ENABLED=0

# Primary engine: claude | codex  (blank = claude)
ENGINE=claude

# Router alternation: 1 = alternate Claude<->Codex when both have headroom
ROUTER_ALTERNATE=1

# Tier ladder: 1 = round-robin model/effort within a MIN..MAX range (saves tokens)
ROUTER_TIER_LADDER=1
# Claude model ladder, cheapest first (comma-sep)
CLAUDE_TIER_LADDER=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001,claude-sonnet-5
# Codex effort ladder, cheapest first (comma-sep)
CODEX_TIER_LADDER=low,medium

# Claude model override (blank = engine default)
MODEL=
# Claude reasoning effort: low | medium | high  (blank = default)
CLAUDE_EFFORT=
# Codex reasoning effort: low | medium | high  (blank = codex default; operator cap = high)
CODEX_EFFORT=

# Seconds between loop cycles
LOOP_INTERVAL=900

# ── APP-263 four-gate budget model (ALL values notional/API-equivalent USD, ──
# ── never billed cash; ccusage prices what the tokens would have cost).     ──
# Per-engine 5h gates: one engine at its cap pauses ONLY that engine.
CLAUDE_5H_BUDGET_USD=100
CODEX_5H_BUDGET_USD=100
# TOTAL hard gates: at the cap BOTH engines pause. Daily = UTC calendar day;
# Weekly = rolling 7x24h, spend expires entry-by-entry.
TOTAL_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=500
TOTAL_WEEKLY_BUDGET_USD=2500
# A blank gate = that gate off. ALL FOUR blank = unbounded spend (boot warns).
# The loop LATCHES (logs/LOOP_HOLD, operator-cleared) whenever it cannot
# measure spend: ccusage failure with no prior observation, an unwritable or
# malformed ledger, a cycle with zero/N-A/unparseable cost.

# ── Harness split (jcode cutover). Provider-level: ─────────────────────────
#   LOOP_HARNESS        claude cycles:  cli (default) | jcode
#   LOOP_HARNESS_CODEX  codex  cycles:  cli (default) | jcode
# Approved production split is claude→jcode, codex→cli (codex stays on the CLI:
# its enabled_tools allowlist is kept and no second OpenAI credential file has
# to coexist with the analyst's). Rollback = LOOP_HARNESS=cli + restart.
LOOP_HARNESS=cli
LOOP_HARNESS_CODEX=cli
# jcode state dir — MUST live on the persistent volume (container FS is
# replaced every redeploy; an ephemeral HOME silently kills jcode's OpenAI
# credential file). Only read when a harness above is 'jcode'.
JCODE_HOME=/app/logs/.jcode
# Tool surface for jcode cycles (defaults live in auto-loop.sh; the boot probe
# verifies the deny list against the live servers and the manifest):
# JCODE_TOOLS_DENY=...        # override only with operator sign-off
# NOTE: JCODE_MCP_PROBE is RETIRED — the deterministic MCP probe is mandatory
# and has no bypass (REVISE-2 gate B11). Do not set it.

# DEPRECATED (ignored; boot logs a warning if set): WINDOW_BUDGET_USD,
# TOTAL_BUDGET_USD, PLAN_CEILING_USD, OPERATOR_RESERVE_PCT, WINDOW_BUDGET_FLOOR_USD
WINDOW_BUDGET_USD=
# Codex cycles per window (blank = unmetered)
CODEX_WINDOW_LIMIT=
# Pause when budget hit and Codex unavailable (seconds)
BUDGET_PAUSE_SECONDS=

# ccusage (cockpit Cost panel — cross-agent API-EQUIVALENT $ estimate incl. Codex).
# Optional; the panel fails open if ccusage is missing. `ccusage` ships in the image.
# CCUSAGE_CMD=ccusage          # command (e.g. "npx --yes ccusage@latest" to skip install)
# CCUSAGE_WINDOW_DAYS=30       # trailing days to aggregate
# CCUSAGE_TTL_SECONDS=600      # cache TTL; recomputed in a background thread when stale

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS / credentials — fill on deploy, NEVER commit real values.
# (Left blank/commented here on purpose. Store via Keychain->runtime.env
#  or as Coolify env vars.)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# LLM engine auth
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=      # headless Claude token (`claude setup-token`)
# CODEX_AUTH_B64=              # base64 of Codex auth.json (optional Codex fallback)

# Integrations the loop reads/writes (headless-safe, via .mcp.json ${VAR})
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=            # Context7 docs MCP (today provided via Coolify env)
# AIRTABLE_API_KEY=           # Airtable PAT, base-scoped to appPLc31jSlgulX3D (APP-230)
# LINEAR_API_KEY=             # Linear personal API key, team APP (APP-230)

# Operator channel (Telegram per-cycle ping — APP-227)
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Comms / outreach (Twilio Email+SMS+WhatsApp+Voice — APP-211/212/213)
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_API_SID=
# TWILIO_API_SECRET=

# Deploy / self-redeploy (Coolify — see redeploy runbook)
# COOLIFY_URL=https://app.coolify.io
# COOLIFY_APP_UUID=
# COOLIFY_DEPLOY_TOKEN=        # Coolify token format is  id|secret  (the `|` is why
#                             #  the entrypoint parses literally, never `. source`)

# Company git identity (for the company's own deploys, separate from the operator)
# GH_TOKEN=
# COMPANY_GIT_NAME=
# COMPANY_GIT_EMAIL=
